+// Block-rounded fp16 matmul: ``out[..., m, n]`` is the sum over 16-wide K
+// blocks of ``fp16(accumulate_fp32(x[..., block] * weight[n * K + block]))``
+// with each block's fp32 partial rounded to fp16 and the blocks
+// accumulated in fp16 ascending order. ``weight`` is a 1-D fp16 array of
+// ``N * K`` elements (the row-major ``[N, K]`` matrix flattened), K must be
+// a positive multiple of 16, and both operands must be fp16. On backends
+// without the fused kernel this falls back to a single fp32-accumulated
+// matmul rounded once, which is NOT the block-rounded contract.
+MLX_API array block_rounded_matmul(
+    const array& x,
+    const array& weight,
+    StreamOrDevice s = {});
+
